WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.248
LLM threat modeling adapts traditional security engineering to AI-powered applications.

2
00:00:05.248 --> 00:00:21.741
Teams should map system components, data flows, and trust boundaries; identify assets and security goals; analyze traditional and AI-specific threats; write concrete abuse cases; select layered controls; and keep the threat model updated as the system changes.

3
00:00:21.741 --> 00:00:38.912
Important risks include prompt injection, indirect prompt injection, sensitive data disclosure, retrieval poisoning, memory poisoning, insecure output handling, excessive tool permissions, unsafe automation, and overreliance on model output.

4
00:00:38.912 --> 00:00:46.885
Strong LLM security depends on architecture, controls, testing, monitoring, and ongoing review, not prompting alone.
